#: functions/bitops.xml:5
msgid "Bit Operations"
msgstr "Operåcions pa bite"

#: functions/bitops.xml:11 functions/bitops.xml:30 functions/bitops.xml:48
#: functions/bitops.xml:66 functions/bitops.xml:85 functions/math.xml:71
#: functions/math.xml:92
msgid "First number"
msgstr "Prumî limero"

#: functions/bitops.xml:15 functions/bitops.xml:70 functions/bitops.xml:89
#: functions/math.xml:75 functions/math.xml:96
msgid "Second number"
msgstr "Deujhinme limero"

#: functions/bitops.xml:19
msgid ""
"The BITAND() function performs a bit-wise AND operation for the two integer "
"parameters."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion BITAND() fwait ene operåcion ET bit-a-bit po les deus parametes "
"etirs"

#: functions/bitops.xml:20
msgid "BITAND(value; value)"
msgstr "BITAND(valixhance; valixhance)"

#: functions/bitops.xml:21
msgid ""
"BITAND(12;10) returns 8 (because decimal 12 is binary 1100, and decimal 10 "
"is binary 1010; and 1100 \"anded\" with 1010 is 1000, which is integer 8)."
msgstr ""
"BITAND(12;10) ritoûne 8 (a cåze kel decimå 12 is binaire 1100 eyet l' decimå "
"10 est binaire 1010 eyet 1100 \"eté\" avou 1010 ça dene 1000, ki si etir est "
"8)."

#: functions/bitops.xml:34
msgid "Amount to left shift by"
msgstr "Cwantité k' on displaece viè l' hintche"

#: functions/bitops.xml:38
msgid ""
"The BITLSHIFT() function performs a bit-wise left shift operation of the "
"first parameter. The number of bits to shift by is specified by the second "
"parameter. Note that a negative number of bits to left shift by becomes a "
"right shift. "
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion BITLSHIFT() fwait ene operåcion d' displaeçaedje bit-a-bit viè "
"l' hintche do prumî paramete. Li nombe di bits k' on va displaecî est "
"specifyî pal deujhinme paramete. Notez k' on nombe negatif di bits a "
"displaecî viè l' hintche divént on displaeçaedje viè l' droete."

#: functions/bitops.xml:39
msgid "BITLSHIFT(value; shift size)"
msgstr "BITLSHIFT(valixhance; grandeu do displaeçaedje)"

#: functions/bitops.xml:52
msgid "Amount to right shift by"
msgstr "Cwantité k' on displaece viè l' droete"

#: functions/bitops.xml:56
msgid ""
"The BITRSHIFT() function performs a bit-wise right shift operation of the "
"first parameter. The number of bits to shift by is specified by the second "
"parameter. Note that a negative number of bits to right shift by becomes a "
"left shift. "
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion BITRSHIFT() fwait ene operåcion d' displaeçaedje bit-a-bit viè "
"l' droete do prumî paramete. Li nombe di bits k' on va displaecî est "
"specifyî pal deujhinme paramete. Notez k' on nombe negatif di bits a "
"displaecî viè l' droete divént on displaeçaedje viè l' hintche."

#: functions/bitops.xml:57
msgid "BITRSHIFT(value; shift size)"
msgstr "BITRSHIFT(valixhance; grandeu do displaeçaedje)"

#: functions/bitops.xml:74
msgid ""
"The BITOR() function performs a bit-wise OR operation for the two integer "
"parameters. "
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion BITOR() fwait ene operåcion OU bit-a-bit po les deus parametes "
"etirs."

#: functions/bitops.xml:75
msgid "BITOR(value; value)"
msgstr "BITOR(valixhance; valixhance)"

#: functions/bitops.xml:76
msgid ""
"BITOR(12;10) returns 14 (because decimal 12 is binary 1100, and decimal 10 "
"is binary 1010; and 1100 \"ored\" with 1010 is 1110, which is integer 14)."
msgstr ""
"BITOR(12;10) ritoûne 14 (a cåze kel decimå 12 est l' binaire 1100 eyet kel "
"decimå 10 est l' binaire 1010 eyet k' 1100 \"ouwé\" avou 1010 ça dene 1110, "
"ki si etir est 14)."

#: functions/bitops.xml:93
msgid ""
"The BITXOR() function performs a bit-wise exclusive-OR operation for the two "
"integer parameters. "
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion BITXOR() fwait ene operåcion seulmint OU (SOU) bit-a-bit po les "
"deus paramete etirs."

#: functions/bitops.xml:94
msgid "BITXOR(value; value)"
msgstr "BITXOR(valixhance; valixhance)"

#: functions/bitops.xml:95
msgid ""
"BITXOR(12;10) returns 6 (because decimal 12 is binary 1100, and decimal 10 "
"is binary 1010; and 1100 \"xored\" with 1010 is 0110, which is integer 6)."
msgstr ""
"BITXOR(12;10) ritoûne 6 (a cåze kel decimå 12 est l' binaire 1100 eyet kel "
"decimå 10 est l' binaire 1010 eyet k' 1100 \"souwé\" avou 1010 ça dene 0110, "
"ki si etir est 6)."

#: functions/conversion.xml:5
msgid "Conversion"
msgstr "Coviertixhaedje"

#: functions/conversion.xml:11 functions/conversion.xml:44
msgid "Bool value to convert"
msgstr "Valixhance bouleyinne a covierser"

#: functions/conversion.xml:15
msgid ""
"The BOOL2STRING() function returns a string value for a given boolean value. "
"This method is intended for using a boolean in methods which require a string"
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion BOOL2STRING() ritoûne ene valixhance tchinne pos ene dinêye "
"bouleyinne di dnêye. Cisse metôde est fwaite pos eployî dins les metôdes k' "
"ont dandjî d' ene tchinne"

#: functions/conversion.xml:16
msgid "BOOL2STRING(value)"
msgstr "BOOL2STRING(valixhance)"

#: functions/conversion.xml:17
msgid "BOOL2STRING(true) returns \"True\""
msgstr "BOOL2STRING(true) tiroûne \"Vraiy\""

#: functions/conversion.xml:18
msgid "BOOL2STRING(false) returns \"False\""
msgstr "BOOL2STRING(false) ritoûne \"Fås\""

#: functions/conversion.xml:19
msgid "upper(BOOL2STRING(find(\"nan\";\"banana\"))) returns TRUE"
msgstr "upper(BOOL2STRING(find(\"nan\";\"banana\"))) ritoûne VRAIY"

#: functions/conversion.xml:27
msgid "Integer value to convert"
msgstr "Etire valixhance a covierser"

#: functions/conversion.xml:31
msgid ""
"The INT2BOOL() function returns a boolean value for a given integer number. "
"This method is intended for using an integer in methods which require a "
"boolean. It only accepts 0 or 1. If any other value is given, false is "
"returned."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion INT2BOOL() ritoûne ene valixhance bouleyinne pos on nombe etir "
"diné. Cisse metôde est fwaite po s' siervi d' en etir dins des metôdes k' "
"ont dandjî d' on bouleyin. Ele ni prind k' les 0 et les 1. Si tolminme kene "
"ôte valixhance est dnêye, ele rioûne fås."

#: functions/conversion.xml:32
msgid "INT2BOOL(value)"
msgstr "INT2BOOL(valixhance)"

#: functions/conversion.xml:33
msgid "INT2BOOL(1) returns true"
msgstr "INT2BOOL(1) ritoûne vraiy"

#: functions/conversion.xml:34
msgid "INT2BOOL(0) returns false"
msgstr "INT2BOOL(0) ritoûne fås"

#: functions/conversion.xml:35
msgid "OR(INT2BOOL(1); false) returns true"
msgstr "OR(INT2BOOL(1); false) ritoûne fås"

#: functions/conversion.xml:48
msgid ""
"The BOOL2INT() function returns an integer value for a given boolean value. "
"This method is intended for using a boolean value in methods which require "
"an integer."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion BOOL2INT() ritoûne ene valixhance etire pos ene valixhance "
"bouleyinne di dné. Cisse metôde est fwaite pos eployî ene valixhance "
"bouleyinne dins des metôdes k' ont dandjî d' en etir."

#: functions/conversion.xml:49
msgid "BOOL2INT(value)"
msgstr "BOOL2INT(valixhance)"

#: functions/conversion.xml:50
msgid "BOOL2INT(True) returns 1"
msgstr "BOOL2INT(True) ritoûne 1"

#: functions/conversion.xml:51
msgid "BOOL2INT(False) returns 0"
msgstr "BOOL2INT(False) ritoûne 0"

#: functions/conversion.xml:60 functions/conversion.xml:77
msgid "Number to convert into string"
msgstr "Nombe a covierser e tchinne"

#: functions/conversion.xml:64
